From 485d6b77515a9d4000b9a54daa5eb5068209eebc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 15:50:17 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(setup): move B3 guarantees onto the LIVE lib setup path

Adversarial review found 2 of B3's 3 guarantees had landed on bin/forge.js's LEGACY/DEAD
installGitHooks/autoInstallLefthook (the registry command in lib/commands/setup.js wins the
dispatcher and returns before bin's inline setup branch runs). Move/repair them on the live path:

- F1a LOUD FAILURE (live): lib installGitHooks now takes { loud }. quickSetup + executeSetup
  call it loud -> banner + process.exitCode=1 when a git repo's hooks end up inert (was: one
  console.warn + exit 0). Mid-stage repairRuntimeReadiness stays quiet.
- F1b ANCESTOR GUARD (live): lib autoInstallLefthook now skips the package-manager lefthook
  install when projectRoot has no package.json (kernel 22e33dbf) - native hooks back enforcement.
- F2 INIT FALLBACK: ensureGitHooksInstalled no longer early-returns on a missing package.json,
  so `forge init` on a bare repo runs the native .git/hooks fallback instead of getting zero hooks.
- F3 core.hooksPath: resolveGitHooksDir now asks `git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-path
  hooks` first (honors core.hooksPath / husky / global config), filesystem logic as fallback - so
  verify checks (and native install writes to) the dir git actually executes. Kills a false-pass.

Tests: retargeted setup-native-fallback-wiring.test.js at lib/commands/setup.js (was asserting the
dead bin functions) + added 3 real end-to-end runs of the actual `forge setup` handler: (a) inert
git repo exits NON-ZERO + loud; (b) `forge setup --yes` bare repo installs native hooks, no pkg-mgr
install; (c) `forge setup --quick` bare repo hits the ancestor guard. Fixed the lefthook-wiring
docstring that mislabeled bin as the live path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
